   "use": "Used to ask about and describe drinking: osake nomu? or osake nomeru? (do you drink?), anmari nomanai (I don't drink much). Casual speech drops o, and once drinking is the topic nomu alone means alcohol: kinou nomisugita (I drank too much last night).",
   "notes": "nomi ni iku (go out for drinks) and nomikai (a drinking party) use the same nomu. How much you can take is osake ni tsuyoi / osake ni yowai, casually osake yowai n da (I'm a lightweight). Bare sake (sake nomou ze) is rougher, mostly male speech; osake is the everyday default for everyone.",
   "example": {
    "romaji": "kyou kuruma da kara, osake wa nomenai.",
