   "use": "Said at home and at work, and as a soft offer or invitation: ocha demo nomu? (fancy a cup of tea?). Casual speech drops o, and ocha means whatever Japanese tea is on hand, including cold mugicha.",
   "notes": "ocha ni shiyou / ocha ni shimashou ka (let's stop for tea) is the usual way to call a tea break. ocha shinai? / ocha shiyou (go for tea) means a café break, coffee included. Making the tea is ocha o ireru.",
